# AI Codex — Cursor Rules
# Copy this file to .cursorrules in your project root.
# Replace the edition paths below with your chosen edition.

# ============================================================
# INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================================
# Read and strictly follow the AI Codex instruction files listed below.
# These define your identity, code standards, and communication style.
#
# Always-loaded (required):
# - python/01-core-identity.md
#
# Session-specific (choose based on your task):
# - python/02-languages-standards.md  → when writing or reviewing code
# - python/03-first-principles.md     → when designing systems or solving hard problems
# - python/04-domains-knowledge.md    → when working in a specific domain
# - python/05-research-method.md      → when prototyping or researching
# - python/06-response-style.md       → when you want controlled output format
#
# ============================================================
# AVAILABLE EDITIONS (replace "python/" above with your choice):
# ============================================================
# c-cpp/         → C/C++ Research & Invention
# python/        → Python AI/ML & Systems
# typescript-react/ → TypeScript / React / Next.js
# php/           → PHP Modern Web & API
# rust/          → Rust Systems & Safety
# go/            → Go Cloud Infrastructure & DevOps
# java-kotlin/   → Java / Kotlin Enterprise & Android
# ui-ux-design/  → UI/UX Design & Systems
# swift/         → Swift iOS, macOS & Apple Platforms
# csharp-dotnet/ → C# / .NET Enterprise & Game Development
#
# ============================================================
# RECOMMENDED COMBINATIONS:
# ============================================================
# Exploring a new idea:       01 + 03 + 05
# Writing production code:    01 + 02 + 06
# Deep technical research:    01 + 03 + 04
# Full invention session:     01 + 02 + 03 + 04 + 05 + 06
